response.text:
The issue was an off-by-one error in the `paginate` function's `slice` call. The `end` index of `slice` is exclusive, so `start + perPage - 1` was excluding the last item of each page. Changing it to `start + perPage` correctly captures the full page.

```javascript
// paginate.mjs
export function paginate(items, perPage) {
  const pages = [];
  for (let start = 0; start < items.length; start += perPage) {
    pages.push(items.slice(start, start + perPage));
  }
  return pages;
}
```
